<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polyaenus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Polyaenus was a Macedonian rhetorician and writer of the second century CE who lived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Around 163 he dedicated to the emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-aurelius">Marcus Aurelius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-verus">Lucius Verus</a> his Stratagems, a collection of some 900 ruses of war drawn from Greek, Roman and barbarian history, meant to help them in the Parthian war. The work preserves many stories from lost historians.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polyaenus.jpg" alt="Polyaenus" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: I curatori del libro · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miniatura_degli_Stratagemmi_di_Polieno.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
